{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HaHCzESqn8AsoDMBH8PiNs","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tnarrative_guidance: 'Pairwise confusability signal 跨任务复现但效应量偏小（r=0.11-0.13），FewRel\n2\t  Δ=-31pp 是 headline 但被部分 reviewer 质疑为 RE-specific。Error taxonomy 无争议（A2 成立）。SDGD\n3\t  全线负面， \"no practical method\" 是 1-2 位 reviewer 的 major weakness。LLaMA Few-NERD 多次失败是  generalizability\n4\t  短板。MAVEN per-type 正方向需更强的 centrality confound 定量论证。 整体落入 Findings 或需 rebuttal 挽救。\n5\t\n6\t  '\n7\timagined_experiments:\n8\t- name: DocRED Confusability Study\n9\t  plan_id: exp-005\n10\t  description: DocRED 96 relation types count curve + BCS 控制实验，跨 NER→sentRE→docRE\n11\t    验证\n12\t  expected_results:\n13\t    count_curve:\n14\t      count_1_acc: 0.74\n15\t      count_4_acc: 0.66\n16\t      count_8_acc: 0.59\n17\t      count_16_acc: 0.48\n18\t      count_32_acc: 0.43\n19\t      count_64_acc: 0.36\n20\t      count_96_acc: 0.32\n21\t      degradation_pp: -42.0\n22\t    bcs_controlled_count16:\n23\t      low_bcs_acc: 0.56\n24\t      high_bcs_acc: 0.4\n25\t      delta_pp: -16.0\n26\t      spearman_r: -0.42\n27\t      spearman_p: 0.028\n28\t    bcs_controlled_count32:\n29\t      low_bcs_acc: 0.5\n30\t      high_bcs_acc: 0.37\n31\t      delta_pp: -13.0\n32\t      spearman_r: -0.36\n33\t      spearman_p: 0.055\n34\t    pairwise_scs_confusion:\n35\t      pearson_r: 0.09\n36\t      ci_95:\n37\t      - 0.04\n38\t      - 0.14\n39\t      n_pairs: 4560\n40\t  result_rationale: 'DocRED 是 document-level RE，baseline 比 sentence-level FewRel 低\n41\t    ~12pp（跨句推理、 多 entity-pair 干扰）。Count curve 退化 42pp，与 FewRel 80-rel 的 35pp 量级一致但\n42\t    更大——96 types + document-level complexity 双重加剧。BCS 效应 Δ=-16pp 存在但弱于  FewRel 的 -31pp：document-level\n43\t    的每篇文档含多个 entity pairs，relation 决策受  entity pair distance、跨句推理等非 confusability\n44\t    因素影响，稀释了纯 BCS 信号。 Pairwise r=0.09 刚好显著（CI 排除零但上界仅 0.14），reviewer 会质疑 document-level  增加的噪声源是否被充分控制。count_32\n45\t    p=0.055 刚好不显著，给 reviewer 留下\"cherry-pick  count 条件\"的把柄。Median 档位下，DocRED 提供\"方向一致但不具决定性\"的第四任务证据。\n46\t\n47\t    '\n48\t  tables:\n49\t  - name: 'Table: DocRED Count Curve (Qwen3-32B)'\n50\t    content: '| Count | Acc   | BCS_mean | N_batches |\n51\t\n52\t      |-------|-------|----------|-----------|\n53\t\n54\t      | 1     | 0.740 | 0        | 96        |\n55\t\n56\t      | 4     | 0.660 | 0.53     | 5         |\n57\t\n58\t      | 8     | 0.590 | 0.64     | 5         |\n59\t\n60\t      | 16    | 0.480 | 0.73     | 5         |\n61\t\n62\t      | 32    | 0.430 | 0.83     | 5         |\n63\t\n64\t      | 64    | 0.360 | 0.91     | 5         |\n65\t\n66\t      | 96    | 0.320 | 0.95     | 5         |\n67\t\n68\t      '\n69\t  - name: 'Table: DocRED BCS-Controlled'\n70\t    content: '| Count | Low-BCS Acc | High-BCS Acc | Δ(pp)  | ρ     | p     |\n71\t\n72\t      |-------|-------------|--------------|--------|-------|-------|\n73\t\n74\t      | 16    | 0.560       | 0.400        | -16.0  | -0.42 | 0.028 |\n75\t\n76\t      | 32    | 0.500       | 0.370        | -13.0  | -0.36 | 0.055 |\n77\t\n78\t      '\n79\t  figures_description:\n80\t  - 'Count curve: monotonic decline 0.74→0.32，steepest segment 8→16'\n81\t  - 'BCS-accuracy scatter (count=16): negative slope 但置信带较宽'\n82\t  analysis: '方向复现但信号偏弱。Reviewer 会指出：(1) count_32 p 值 borderline；(2) document-level  引入未控制的\n83\t    confound（entity pair distance, 跨句推理）；(3) pairwise r=0.09 低于  Few-NERD/MAVEN 的\n84\t    0.11-0.13。Rebuttal 需强调 harder setting 下方向一致的价值， 并补充 entity-pair distance 控制分析。\n85\t\n86\t    '\n87\t- name: Interaction Effect 2×2\n88\t  plan_id: exp-006\n89\t  description: '{low/high count} × {low/high BCS} 检验 count 和 confusability 的交互效应'\n90\t  expected_results:\n91\t    cell_means_f1:\n92\t      low_count_low_bcs: 0.324\n93\t      low_count_high_bcs: 0.313\n94\t      high_count_low_bcs: 0.325\n95\t      high_count_high_bcs: 0.277\n96\t    main_effect_count_pp: -1.8\n97\t    main_effect_bcs_pp: -2.9\n98\t    interaction_z: -0.67\n99\t    interaction_p: 0.5\n100\t    bcs_effect_at_low_count_pp: -1.1\n101\t    bcs_effect_at_high_count_pp: -4.8\n102\t  result_rationale: '交互方向符合 multiplicative 假设（高 count 下 BCS 效应 4.4× 于低 count），但  p=0.50\n103\t    远不显著。根本原因是 Few-NERD 实验设计的固有限制：(1) count 对比仅 6 vs 12， 差异过小（FewRel 的 3.4× amplification\n104\t    用的是 16 vs 80）；(2) BCS 范围窄  (0.75-0.90)，Few-NERD 66 types 中高相似度集中在 person 子类、location\n105\t    子类； (3) n=27 per cell，power analysis 估计需 n≈80 才能在此效应量下达到 0.8 power。 这不是假设被否定——是实验\n106\t    underpowered。但 median 档 reviewer 不会区分 \"underpowered  null\" 和 \"true null\"，会标注为\n107\t    \"interaction claim not supported\"。\n108\t\n109\t    '\n110\t  tables:\n111\t  - name: 'Table: 2×2 Interaction Design (Few-NERD F1)'\n112\t    content: '|              | Low BCS | High BCS | BCS Δ  |\n113\t\n114\t      |--------------|---------|----------|--------|\n115\t\n116\t      | Count=6      | 0.324   | 0.313    | -0.011 |\n117\t\n118\t      | Count=12     | 0.325   | 0.277    | -0.048 |\n119\t\n120\t      | Count Δ      | +0.001  | -0.036   |        |\n121\t\n122\t      | Interaction: z=-0.67, p=0.50 (n.s.)        |\n123\t\n124\t      '\n125\t  figures_description:\n126\t  - 'Interaction plot: 两条线（low/high BCS）跨 count 水平，方向 non-parallel 但 CI 大量重叠'\n127\t  analysis: '需要在论文中如实报告 null result 并提供 power analysis。FewRel 16→80 的 3.4×  amplification\n128\t    作为 indirect interaction evidence。Reviewer 可能要求在 80-rel pool  上做正式 2×2 作为 rebuttal\n129\t    补充分析。\n130\t\n131\t    '\n132\t- name: Error Taxonomy\n133\t  plan_id: exp-007\n134\t  description: 系统性 FP 分类跨 BCS bins，multi-channel 机械性证据\n135\t  expected_results:\n136\t    fewnerd_intra_sub_by_bcs:\n137\t      bcs_zero_pct: 0.0\n138\t      bcs_low_pct: 1.6\n139\t      bcs_medium_pct: 10.6\n140\t      bcs_high_pct: 49.4\n141\t      rho: 1.0\n142\t      p: <0.001\n143\t    fewrel_intra_sub_by_bcs:\n144\t      bcs_zero_pct: 0.0\n145\t      bcs_low_pct: 4.2\n146\t      bcs_medium_pct: 13.0\n147\t      bcs_high_pct: 20.3\n148\t      bcs_very_high_pct: 32.3\n149\t      rho: 0.954\n150\t      p: <1e-6\n151\t    cross_task:\n152\t      ner_rho: 1.0\n153\t      re_rho: 0.954\n154\t    extra_sub: 0.0\n155\t    hallucination_pct: <3%\n156\t    missed_rate_range: 10-16%\n157\t  result_rationale: 'Error taxonomy 是 median 档中最无争议的证据（A2 完全成立）。IntraSub 与 BCS 的  perfect/near-perfect\n158\t    monotonic 关系直接验证了 multi-channel model 的核心机制： confusability 导致 type confusion（IntraSub）而非\n159\t    detection failure（missed rate  不变 10-16%）。几个关键支撑点：(1) extra_sub=0，type confusion\n160\t    严格是 intra-batch  现象，模型只从当前 schema 中选类型；(2) hallucination<3%，LLM 的主错误模式是  \"选错类型\"\n161\t    而非 \"编造实体\"；(3) cross-task replication 几乎完美（NER ρ=1.0,  RE ρ=0.954），同一机制跨 NER 和\n162\t    RE。即使在 median 档位，reviewer 也不会质疑这个分析。 这是论文的 \"safe anchor\"。\n163\t\n164\t    '\n165\t  tables:\n166\t  - name: 'Table: Error Taxonomy — Few-NERD (NER)'\n167\t    content: '| BCS Bin  | N_FP | IntraSub% | ExtraSub% | Other%  |\n168\t\n169\t      |----------|------|-----------|-----------|---------|\n170\t\n171\t      | 0        | 6172 | 0.0       | 90.3      | 9.7     |\n172\t\n173\t      | Low      | 2231 | 1.6       | 89.9      | 8.5     |\n174\t\n175\t      | Medium   | 3843 | 10.6      | 78.1      | 11.3    |\n176\t\n177\t      | High     | 6188 | 49.4      | 30.8      | 19.8    |\n178\t\n179\t      '\n180\t  - name: 'Table: Error Taxonomy — FewRel 80-rel (RE)'\n181\t    content: '| BCS Bin    | Correct% | IntraSub% | Missed% |\n182\t\n183\t      |------------|----------|-----------|---------|\n184\t\n185\t      | Zero       | 85.7     | 0.0       | 14.3    |\n186\t\n187\t      | Low        | 85.4     | 4.2       | 10.4    |\n188\t\n189\t      | Medium     | 75.7     | 13.0      | 11.3    |\n190\t\n191\t      | High       | 66.7     | 20.3      | 13.0    |\n192\t\n193\t      | Very High  | 52.0     | 32.3      | 15.7    |\n194\t\n195\t      '\n196\t  - name: 'Table: Cross-task Monotonicity'\n197\t    content: '| Task | IntraSub vs BCS ρ | p       |\n198\t\n199\t      |------|-------------------|---------|\n200\t\n201\t      | NER  | 1.000             | <0.001  |\n202\t\n203\t      | RE   | 0.954             | <1e-6   |\n204\t\n205\t      '\n206\t  figures_description:\n207\t  - 'Stacked bar: FP composition 从 ExtraSub-dominant (BCS=0) 翻转为 IntraSub-dominant\n208\t    (BCS>0.95)'\n209\t  - 'Cross-task overlay: NER 和 RE IntraSub curves 近乎平行上升'\n210\t  analysis: '论文最强的机械性证据，也是 Claim 2 的核心支撑。Cross-task ρ={1.0, 0.954} 是整篇论文 中最具说服力的数字。Median\n211\t    档 reviewer 对此无异议。建议在论文中将此作为 Section 4  的第一个分析呈现（先建立机制理解，再展示 pairwise/scaling 证据）。\n212\t\n213\t    '\n214\t- name: SDGD-zero on MAVEN\n215\t  plan_id: exp-009\n216\t  description: SDGD-zero 在 MAVEN 168 event types 上测试，对比 single-pass + random\n217\t  expected_results:\n218\t    single_pass:\n219\t      relaxed_f1: 0.247\n220\t      precision: 0.32\n221\t      recall: 0.2\n222\t      batches: 1\n223\t      time_s: 130\n224\t    random_batch:\n225\t      relaxed_f1: 0.175\n226\t      precision: 0.14\n227\t      recall: 0.23\n228\t      batches: 12\n229\t      time_s: 950\n230\t    sdgd_zero:\n231\t      relaxed_f1: 0.135\n232\t      precision: 0.12\n233\t      recall: 0.155\n234\t      batches: 8\n235\t      time_s: 680\n236\t    per_type:\n237\t      relaxed_f1: 0.11\n238\t      precision: 0.07\n239\t      recall: 0.3\n240\t      batches: 168\n241\t      time_s: 9200\n242\t  result_rationale: 'MAVEN 168 types 使所有 decomposition 方法的表现更差，原因层叠：(1) 168 types\n243\t    产生  更多 batches，每次 merge 引入更多冲突——merge amplification 与 batch 数量超线性增长； (2) MAVEN\n244\t    event types 语义高度同质（均为 FrameNet 层级，SCS mean=0.216,  119 pairs>0.5），SDGD-zero 的\n245\t    graph coloring 无法有效分离——色数极高，被迫使用  大量 small batches 或在同 batch 内保留高 SCS pairs；(3)\n246\t    event trigger boundary  本身模糊（exact F1 仅 0.01-0.03），decomposition 后 merge 多个 batch\n247\t    的 trigger  predictions 进一步恶化边界匹配。SDGD-zero F1=0.135 vs single-pass 0.247，退化比 (0.55)\n248\t    与 Few-NERD 上一致 (0.24/0.45=0.53)。Random batch 再次优于 SDGD-zero  (0.175 vs 0.135)——SDGD\n249\t    的不均匀 batch size 在 MAVEN 上伤害更大。Per-type (168 batches)  recall 最高但 precision 崩溃（0.07），9200s\n250\t    延迟不可接受。 Median 档位下，此实验巩固 \"merge amplification 是跨任务的结构性障碍\"，但同时加深  \"no practical\n251\t    method\" 这一 major weakness。\n252\t\n253\t    '\n254\t  tables:\n255\t  - name: 'Table: SDGD Comparison — MAVEN 168 types'\n256\t    content: '| Method      | Relaxed F1 | P     | R     | k   | Time(s) |\n257\t\n258\t      |-------------|------------|-------|-------|-----|---------|\n259\t\n260\t      | Single-pass | 0.247      | 0.320 | 0.200 | 1   | 130     |\n261\t\n262\t      | Random      | 0.175      | 0.140 | 0.230 | 12  | 950     |\n263\t\n264\t      | SDGD-zero   | 0.135      | 0.120 | 0.155 | 8   | 680     |\n265\t\n266\t      | Per-type    | 0.110      | 0.070 | 0.300 | 168 | 9200    |\n267\t\n268\t      '\n269\t  figures_description:\n270\t  - 'Bar chart: single-pass 大幅领先，所有 decomposition 方法均为负面'\n271\t  - 'Cross-dataset comparison: Few-NERD vs MAVEN decomposition penalty 一致'\n272\t  analysis: '与 Few-NERD 模式完全一致。论文中应将 Few-NERD + MAVEN 的 SDGD 负面结果并排呈现， 强调 \"decomposition\n273\t    penalty 是 task-agnostic 的结构性问题\"。同时明确指出 merge  strategy 是瓶颈（不是 grouping quality），为\n274\t    future work 指明方向。Reviewer 的核心 质疑仍然是 \"如果你的方法不 work，这篇论文的 practical value 是什么？\"。\n275\t\n276\t    '\n277\t- name: SDGD-cal on Few-NERD\n278\t  plan_id: exp-010\n279\t  description: 基于 5-10 个 calibration examples 的 empirical confusability graph，对比 SDGD-zero\n280\t  expected_results:\n281\t    sdgd_cal_5shot:\n282\t      f1: 0.295\n283\t      precision: 0.34\n284\t      recall: 0.26\n285\t      batches: 5\n286\t      time_s: 370\n287\t      calibration_overhead_s: 50\n288\t    sdgd_cal_10shot:\n289\t      f1: 0.315\n290\t      precision: 0.36\n291\t      recall: 0.28\n292\t      batches: 5\n293\t      time_s: 370\n294\t      calibration_overhead_s: 90\n295\t    vs_baselines:\n296\t      sdgd_zero_f1: 0.241\n297\t      random_batch_f1: 0.301\n298\t      single_pass_f1: 0.445\n299\t      cal5_vs_zero_pp: '+5.4'\n300\t      cal10_vs_zero_pp: '+7.4'\n301\t      cal10_vs_single_pass_pp: '-13.0'\n302\t  result_rationale: 'Calibration 用 empirical confusion matrix 替代 embedding SCS，绕过了\n303\t    embedding  选择问题，直接捕捉模型实际 confusion pattern。改善来源：(1) empirical confusion  比 SCS\n304\t    更准确地识别 true confusion pairs（SCS 只解释 ~3% 方差，empirical 解释更多）； (2) 基于实际错误的 graph\n305\t    更 sparse（大部分 type pairs 从不 confused），graph coloring  产生更均衡的 batches。但仍远低于 single-pass\n306\t    (-13pp) 的原因不变：merge amplification  与 grouping quality 关系不大，是 decomposition 本身的结构性问题——即使完美分组避免了  所有\n307\t    confusion pairs，合并多个 batch 的输出时同一 span 仍会被多个 batch \"认领\"。 5-shot vs 10-shot 差异小（0.295\n308\t    vs 0.315），因为 5 个样本已识别出主要 confusion  clusters（person 子类、location 子类）。Median 档位下，SDGD-cal\n309\t    展示了 \"right  direction\" 但 Δ=+7pp 不构成 practical improvement，reviewer 评价 \"interesting  diagnostically\n310\t    but not actionable\"。\n311\t\n312\t    '\n313\t  tables:\n314\t  - name: 'Table: SDGD-cal vs Baselines (Few-NERD)'\n315\t    content: '| Method        | F1    | P     | R     | k | Extra(s) |\n316\t\n317\t      |---------------|-------|-------|-------|---|----------|\n318\t\n319\t      | Single-pass   | 0.445 | 0.563 | 0.368 | 1 | 0        |\n320\t\n321\t      | Random        | 0.301 | 0.331 | 0.276 | 8 | 0        |\n322\t\n323\t      | SDGD-zero     | 0.241 | 0.324 | 0.191 | 4 | 0        |\n324\t\n325\t      | SDGD-cal (5)  | 0.295 | 0.340 | 0.260 | 5 | 50       |\n326\t\n327\t      | SDGD-cal (10) | 0.315 | 0.360 | 0.280 | 5 | 90       |\n328\t\n329\t      '\n330\t  figures_description:\n331\t  - 'Bar chart: F1 阶梯 SDGD-zero < SDGD-cal ≈ Random << Single-pass'\n332\t  - 'Precision-Recall scatter: 所有 decomposition 方法位于 single-pass 的 Pareto 劣势区'\n333\t  analysis: 'SDGD-cal ≈ Random batch 的事实 is telling：即使用最好的 grouping signal，结果也不比 随机好多少。这进一步证实瓶颈是\n334\t    merge 不是 grouping。论文中应明确写出这个 implication。 Reviewer 的追问：\"为什么不探索 confidence-weighted\n335\t    merge / NMS-style 去重？\"—— 这是合理的 future work 方向，v2 已尝试 confidence-gated 但未奏效，说明问题比  simple\n336\t    filtering 更深。\n337\t\n338\t    '\n339\t- name: SDGD-cal on MAVEN\n340\t  plan_id: exp-011\n341\t  description: SDGD-cal 在 MAVEN 168 types 上的表现\n342\t  expected_results:\n343\t    sdgd_cal_5shot:\n344\t      relaxed_f1: 0.165\n345\t      precision: 0.15\n346\t      recall: 0.185\n347\t      batches: 10\n348\t      calibration_overhead_s: 200\n349\t    sdgd_cal_10shot:\n350\t      relaxed_f1: 0.18\n351\t      precision: 0.17\n352\t      recall: 0.195\n353\t      batches: 10\n354\t      calibration_overhead_s: 380\n355\t    vs_baselines:\n356\t      single_pass_f1: 0.247\n357\t      sdgd_zero_f1: 0.135\n358\t      cal10_vs_zero_pp: '+4.5'\n359\t      cal10_vs_single_pass_pp: '-6.7'\n360\t  result_rationale: 'MAVEN 上 calibration 的边际改善比 Few-NERD 更小（+4.5pp vs +7.4pp），原因：\n361\t    (1) 168 types 的 confusion space 更大（14028 pairs），5-10 个 calibration samples  覆盖率更低——每个\n362\t    sample 最多涉及 ~10 types，需要 O(168) 个 samples 才能充分覆盖； (2) MAVEN 语义同质性导致 confusion\n363\t    graph 极其 dense（几乎所有 type pairs 都有非零  confusion），graph coloring 的 chromatic number\n364\t    很高，无论怎么分组都有大量 high-SCS  pairs 共存；(3) 200-380s 的 calibration overhead 在 168 types\n365\t    上不可忽略，但换来的  仅 4.5pp 改善，投资回报率极低。SDGD-cal 仍远低于 single-pass (-6.7pp)。 Cross-task\n366\t    一致的负面结果强化了结论，但也强化了 \"no practical method\" 的弱点。\n367\t\n368\t    '\n369\t  tables:\n370\t  - name: 'Table: SDGD-cal vs Baselines (MAVEN)'\n371\t    content: '| Method        | Relaxed F1 | k  | Calibration(s) |\n372\t\n373\t      |---------------|------------|----|----------------|\n374\t\n375\t      | Single-pass   | 0.247      | 1  | 0              |\n376\t\n377\t      | Random        | 0.175      | 12 | 0              |\n378\t\n379\t      | SDGD-zero     | 0.135      | 8  | 0              |\n380\t\n381\t      | SDGD-cal (5)  | 0.165      | 10 | 200            |\n382\t\n383\t      | SDGD-cal (10) | 0.180      | 10 | 380            |\n384\t\n385\t      '\n386\t  figures_description:\n387\t  - 'Cross-dataset SDGD comparison: Few-NERD 和 MAVEN bar charts 并排，模式一致'\n388\t  analysis: '建议在论文中将 exp-009 和 exp-011 合并为一个 \"SDGD Results\" subsection，呈现  cross-task\n389\t    一致的 hierarchy: single-pass > random ≈ cal > zero。 明确定位为 \"negative result with\n390\t    diagnostic value\"——理解 WHY decomposition fails  本身是贡献，指向 calibration-aware merge\n391\t    (非 calibration-aware grouping) 作为  correct next step。\n392\t\n393\t    '\n394\t- name: Random Batching Ablation\n395\t  plan_id: exp-013\n396\t  description: 与 SDGD 相同 batch count k 的 random composition，隔离 confusability-aware\n397\t    grouping 的增量\n398\t  expected_results:\n399\t    fewnerd_k4:\n400\t      random_f1: 0.305\n401\t      sdgd_zero_f1: 0.241\n402\t      delta_pp: '+6.4'\n403\t    fewnerd_k8:\n404\t      random_f1: 0.295\n405\t      sdgd_zero_f1: 0.22\n406\t      delta_pp: '+7.5'\n407\t    maven_k8:\n408\t      random_f1: 0.175\n409\t      sdgd_zero_f1: 0.135\n410\t      delta_pp: '+4.0'\n411\t    single_pass_f1_fewnerd: 0.445\n412\t    single_pass_f1_maven: 0.247\n413\t  result_rationale: 'Random batching 在所有条件下优于 SDGD-zero，看似反直觉但有清晰解释： (1) SDGD-zero\n414\t    的 graph coloring + min_batch_size 约束产生高度不均匀的 batch sizes—— 某些 batch 仅含 3-4 types，prompt\n415\t    中类型太少时模型缺乏任务范围 context，对每个类型  过度 predict（high recall, terrible precision）；random\n416\t    batching 的 batch size 更均匀， 避免了这一退化模式；(2) SDGD-zero 将所有 \"hard\" (high-SCS) types\n417\t    集中到同一个  batch，这些 batch 的 precision 崩溃；random 分散了 hard pairs，每个 batch 混合  easy+hard，整体更\n418\t    balanced；(3) confusability-aware grouping 的正确 operationalization  应是 \"将 confusable\n419\t    pairs 分开\"，但 SDGD-zero 的贪心 coloring 在约束下反而集中了  难题。这说明 SDGD-zero 的分组算法有 design flaw，不否定\n420\t    confusability signal 本身。 Median 档位下，\"SDGD-zero < random\" 是 reviewer 最容易攻击的点之一。\n421\t\n422\t    '\n423\t  tables:\n424\t  - name: 'Table: Random vs SDGD-zero Ablation'\n425\t    content: '| Dataset  | k | Random F1 | SDGD-zero F1 | Single-pass F1 |\n426\t\n427\t      |----------|---|-----------|--------------|----------------|\n428\t\n429\t      | Few-NERD | 4 | 0.305     | 0.241        | 0.445          |\n430\t\n431\t      | Few-NERD | 8 | 0.295     | 0.220        | 0.445          |\n432\t\n433\t      | MAVEN    | 8 | 0.175     | 0.135        | 0.247          |\n434\t\n435\t      '\n436\t  figures_description:\n437\t  - 'Bar chart: 三组对比（k=4, k=8, MAVEN k=8），random 始终优于 SDGD-zero'\n438\t  analysis: '关键 takeaway 不是 \"confusability-aware grouping 无用\"，而是 \"当前的 SDGD-zero  实现的分组策略有副作用（batch\n439\t    size 不均匀、hard type 集中化）抵消了 grouping 收益\"。 论文应 (1) 诚实报告 random > SDGD-zero；(2) 分析原因（batch\n440\t    size distribution,  hard-batch concentration）；(3) 指出 all decomposition << single-pass，真正的瓶颈是  merge\n441\t    不是 grouping。Reviewer 可能追问 \"为什么不修复 SDGD 的 batch size 问题？\"—— 合理的 rebuttal 是 exp-010\n442\t    的 SDGD-cal 部分解决了这个问题但仍低于 single-pass。\n443\t\n444\t    '\n445\t- name: Per-type Splitting (UniNER-style)\n446\t  plan_id: exp-014\n447\t  description: 每 batch 仅含 1 type，decomposition 的理论上限\n448\t  expected_results:\n449\t    fewnerd:\n450\t      f1: 0.29\n451\t      precision: 0.195\n452\t      recall: 0.585\n453\t      batches: 66\n454\t      time_s: 2550\n455\t      intra_sub_rate: 0.0\n456\t      recall_vs_single_pass_pp: '+21.7'\n457\t      precision_vs_single_pass_pp: '-36.8'\n458\t      f1_vs_single_pass_pp: '-15.5'\n459\t    maven:\n460\t      relaxed_f1: 0.145\n461\t      precision: 0.085\n462\t      recall: 0.46\n463\t      batches: 168\n464\t      time_s: 9500\n465\t  result_rationale: 'Per-type splitting 完全消除了 type confusion (IntraSub=0)——每个 batch\n466\t    只有一个类型， 不可能把 entity 标为 \"wrong\" type。这验证了 multi-channel model 的 Channel 1 预测： Recall\n467\t    从 0.368 跃升至 0.585 (+21.7pp)，因为每个 prompt 只需关注一个类型， attention 不被稀释，不遗漏。但 Precision\n468\t    从 0.563 崩溃到 0.195 (-36.8pp)—— 66 个 batch 的 union merge 引入大量冲突：同一 text span 被 person-scholar、\n469\t    person-scientist、person-other 各自 \"认领\"，union merge 保留所有 predictions， precision\n470\t    崩溃。F1 净效果为负 (-15.5pp)。 MAVEN 168 types 更极端——recall 高但 precision 更低（0.085），因为 168\n471\t    个 single-type  batch 的 merge 冲突呈 O(k²) 增长。 这清晰展示了 decomposition 的 fundamental\n472\t    tradeoff：分解减少 miss (Channel 1 benefit)， 但 merge 产生 false positives (new Channel\n473\t    3 problem)。当前所有 merge strategy  （union, confidence-gated）都不能解决 O(k) batches 的冲突。\n474\t\n475\t    '\n476\t  tables:\n477\t  - name: 'Table: Full Decomposition Spectrum (Few-NERD)'\n478\t    content: '| Method      | F1    | P     | R     | k  | IntraSub | Time(s) |\n479\t\n480\t      |-------------|-------|-------|-------|----|----------|---------|\n481\t\n482\t      | Single-pass | 0.445 | 0.563 | 0.368 | 1  | baseline | 79      |\n483\t\n484\t      | Random (k=8)| 0.295 | 0.330 | 0.270 | 8  | moderate | 494     |\n485\t\n486\t      | SDGD-zero   | 0.241 | 0.324 | 0.191 | 4  | low      | 261     |\n487\t\n488\t      | SDGD-cal    | 0.315 | 0.360 | 0.280 | 5  | low      | 460     |\n489\t\n490\t      | Per-type    | 0.290 | 0.195 | 0.585 | 66 | 0        | 2550    |\n491\t\n492\t      '\n493\t  figures_description:\n494\t  - 'Precision-Recall tradeoff: per-type 在 high-recall/low-precision 极端，single-pass\n495\t    在 balanced 区'\n496\t  - 'Stacked bar: recall gain vs precision loss，per-type 的 precision loss 完全 dominate'\n497\t  analysis: 'Per-type 的 recall 优势是 decomposition 正确直觉的最好证据——问题确实在 merge。 论文结构建议：先展示\n498\t    per-type 的 recall gain (证明 decomposition 有理论价值)， 再展示所有方法的 precision collapse (证明\n499\t    merge amplification 是瓶颈)， 最后指出 \"future work needs better merge, not better grouping\"。\n500\t    Reviewer 会欣赏这个清晰的 ablation 分析。1-2 位 reviewer 仍会标注 \"the paper  identifies the problem\n501\t    but doesn''t solve it\" 作为 major weakness，这是 median 档 避不开的。\n502\t\n503\t    '\n504\t- name: SCS Validation\n505\t  plan_id: exp-015\n506\t  description: Spearman/Kendall correlation between embedding SCS 和 empirical confusion\n507\t    matrix\n508\t  expected_results:\n509\t    all_pairs:\n510\t      n: 1953\n511\t      qwen3_spearman: 0.168\n512\t      qwen3_p: '7.3e-14'\n513\t      qwen3_kendall: 0.135\n514\t      minilm_spearman: 0.144\n515\t      minilm_p: '1.7e-10'\n516\t      minilm_kendall: 0.115\n517\t    nonzero_only:\n518\t      n: 216\n519\t      qwen3_spearman: 0.272\n520\t      qwen3_p: '5.0e-5'\n521\t      qwen3_kendall: 0.2\n522\t      minilm_spearman: 0.306\n523\t      minilm_p: '4.6e-6'\n524\t      minilm_kendall: 0.228\n525\t    variance_explained:\n526\t      all_pairs_r_squared: 2.8-4.8%\n527\t      nonzero_r_squared: 7.4-9.4%\n528\t  result_rationale: 'SCS 是有效但不完美的 confusion proxy。All-pairs ρ 偏低（0.14-0.17）的根本原因是  data\n529\t    极度 zero-inflated：88.9% 的 type pairs 从未被混淆（confusion=0），产生大量  ties 压缩 rank correlation。Nonzero-only\n530\t    ρ 跳升到 0.27-0.31，说明 SCS 能有效区分  \"哪些 pairs 被混淆得更多\" 但不太能预测 \"哪些 pairs 会被混淆\"。 Qwen3\n531\t    在 all-pairs 上更好（ρ=0.168 vs 0.144）——extraction model 的 embedding  更好地捕捉 \"是否会混淆\"\n532\t    的 threshold，因为 embedding space 与 model 的 internal  representation 对齐。MiniLM 在\n533\t    nonzero-only 上更好（ρ=0.306 vs 0.272）——sentence  similarity model 的 fine-grained\n534\t    similarity gradient 更平滑，更好地排序 confusion  程度。 Median 档位下，reviewer 的主要质疑是 R²=3-5%：如果你的\n535\t    proxy 只解释 3-5% 的方差， 基于它构建的 SDGD 分组怎么可能有效？这恰好与 SDGD-zero 的失败一致——SCS 作为 grouping  signal\n536\t    太 noisy。论文应将此定位为 \"validating the existence of the signal\" 而非  \"validating its\n537\t    practical sufficiency\"，并指向 SDGD-cal (empirical confusion)  作为正确的 operationalization\n538\t    路径。\n539\t\n540\t    '\n541\t  tables:\n542\t  - name: 'Table: SCS → Empirical Confusion Validation'\n543\t    content: '| Subset        | Embedding | Spearman ρ | p        | Kendall τ | R²     |\n544\t\n545\t      |---------------|-----------|------------|----------|-----------|--------|\n546\t\n547\t      | All (n=1953)  | Qwen3     | 0.168      | 7.3e-14  | 0.135     | ~4.8%  |\n548\t\n549\t      | All (n=1953)  | MiniLM    | 0.144      | 1.7e-10  | 0.115     | ~2.8%  |\n550\t\n551\t      | Nonzero (216) | Qwen3     | 0.272      | 5.0e-5   | 0.200     | ~7.4%  |\n552\t\n553\t      | Nonzero (216) | MiniLM    | 0.306      | 4.6e-6   | 0.228     | ~9.4%  |\n554\t\n555\t      '\n556\t  figures_description:\n557\t  - 'SCS vs confusion scatter: 大量零值集中在 x 轴，nonzero 区域显示 positive trend'\n558\t  - 'Embedding 对比: Qwen3 vs MiniLM 的 SCS-confusion curves 在 nonzero 区域交叉'\n559\t  analysis: SCS validation 支撑了 \"confusability signal exists\" 但也暴露了 \"signal is weak\n560\t    for  practical use\"。这与 SDGD 的负面结果形成一致叙事：pairwise SCS 作为分析工具有效 （cross-task 显著），作为工程工具不足（R²太低）。论文应诚实呈现这个\n561\t    gap，并将  SDGD-cal (bypassing embedding entirely) 作为 pragmatic 替代方案。 Reviewer 可能追问\n562\t    AUC（SCS 预测 nonzero confusion 的分类能力），预估 AUC≈0.65-0.70， 属于 \"above chance but far\n563\t    from reliable\" 水平。\n564\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b735db44-76af-4d42-8a6c-987fd4628342","uuid":"c63fc41d-f9a1-4a40-9274-3b3e63bb9c51","timestamp":"2026-05-16T08:12:26.564Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_18/projects/schema-dag-extraction/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260516T073533/median/review_context.yaml","content":"narrative_guidance: 'Pairwise confusability signal 跨任务复现但效应量偏小（r=0.11-0.13），FewRel\n  Δ=-31pp 是 headline 但被部分 reviewer 质疑为 RE-specific。Error taxonomy 无争议（A2 成立）。SDGD\n  全线负面， \"no practical method\" 是 1-2 位 reviewer 的 major weakness。LLaMA Few-NERD 多次失败是  generalizability\n  短板。MAVEN per-type 正方向需更强的 centrality confound 定量论证。 整体落入 Findings 或需 rebuttal 挽救。\n\n  '\nimagined_experiments:\n- name: DocRED Confusability Study\n  plan_id: exp-005\n  description: DocRED 96 relation types count curve + BCS 控制实验，跨 NER→sentRE→docRE\n    验证\n  expected_results:\n    count_curve:\n      count_1_acc: 0.74\n      count_4_acc: 0.66\n      count_8_acc: 0.59\n      count_16_acc: 0.48\n      count_32_acc: 0.43\n      count_64_acc: 0.36\n      count_96_acc: 0.32\n      degradation_pp: -42.0\n    bcs_controlled_count16:\n      low_bcs_acc: 0.56\n      high_bcs_acc: 0.4\n      delta_pp: -16.0\n      spearman_r: -0.42\n      spearman_p: 0.028\n    bcs_controlled_count32:\n      low_bcs_acc: 0.5\n      high_bcs_acc: 0.37\n      delta_pp: -13.0\n      spearman_r: -0.36\n      spearman_p: 0.055\n    pairwise_scs_confusion:\n      pearson_r: 0.09\n      ci_95:\n      - 0.04\n      - 0.14\n      n_pairs: 4560\n  result_rationale: 'DocRED 是 document-level RE，baseline 比 sentence-level FewRel 低\n    ~12pp（跨句推理、 多 entity-pair 干扰）。Count curve 退化 42pp，与 FewRel 80-rel 的 35pp 量级一致但\n    更大——96 types + document-level complexity 双重加剧。BCS 效应 Δ=-16pp 存在但弱于  FewRel 的 -31pp：document-level\n    的每篇文档含多个 entity pairs，relation 决策受  entity pair distance、跨句推理等非 confusability\n    因素影响，稀释了纯 BCS 信号。 Pairwise r=0.09 刚好显著（CI 排除零但上界仅 0.14），reviewer 会质疑 document-level  增加的噪声源是否被充分控制。count_32\n    p=0.055 刚好不显著，给 reviewer 留下\"cherry-pick  count 条件\"的把柄。Median 档位下，DocRED 提供\"方向一致但不具决定性\"的第四任务证据。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: DocRED Count Curve (Qwen3-32B)'\n    content: '| Count | Acc   | BCS_mean | N_batches |\n\n      |-------|-------|----------|-----------|\n\n      | 1     | 0.740 | 0        | 96        |\n\n      | 4     | 0.660 | 0.53     | 5         |\n\n      | 8     | 0.590 | 0.64     | 5         |\n\n      | 16    | 0.480 | 0.73     | 5         |\n\n      | 32    | 0.430 | 0.83     | 5         |\n\n      | 64    | 0.360 | 0.91     | 5         |\n\n      | 96    | 0.320 | 0.95     | 5         |\n\n      '\n  - name: 'Table: DocRED BCS-Controlled'\n    content: '| Count | Low-BCS Acc | High-BCS Acc | Δ(pp)  | ρ     | p     |\n\n      |-------|-------------|--------------|--------|-------|-------|\n\n      | 16    | 0.560       | 0.400        | -16.0  | -0.42 | 0.028 |\n\n      | 32    | 0.500       | 0.370        | -13.0  | -0.36 | 0.055 |\n\n      '\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Count curve: monotonic decline 0.74→0.32，steepest segment 8→16'\n  - 'BCS-accuracy scatter (count=16): negative slope 但置信带较宽'\n  analysis: '方向复现但信号偏弱。Reviewer 会指出：(1) count_32 p 值 borderline；(2) document-level  引入未控制的\n    confound（entity pair distance, 跨句推理）；(3) pairwise r=0.09 低于  Few-NERD/MAVEN 的\n    0.11-0.13。Rebuttal 需强调 harder setting 下方向一致的价值， 并补充 entity-pair distance 控制分析。\n\n    '\n- name: Interaction Effect 2×2\n  plan_id: exp-006\n  description: '{low/high count} × {low/high BCS} 检验 count 和 confusability 的交互效应'\n  expected_results:\n    cell_means_f1:\n      low_count_low_bcs: 0.324\n      low_count_high_bcs: 0.313\n      high_count_low_bcs: 0.325\n      high_count_high_bcs: 0.277\n    main_effect_count_pp: -1.8\n    main_effect_bcs_pp: -2.9\n    interaction_z: -0.67\n    interaction_p: 0.5\n    bcs_effect_at_low_count_pp: -1.1\n    bcs_effect_at_high_count_pp: -4.8\n  result_rationale: '交互方向符合 multiplicative 假设（高 count 下 BCS 效应 4.4× 于低 count），但  p=0.50\n    远不显著。根本原因是 Few-NERD 实验设计的固有限制：(1) count 对比仅 6 vs 12， 差异过小（FewRel 的 3.4× amplification\n    用的是 16 vs 80）；(2) BCS 范围窄  (0.75-0.90)，Few-NERD 66 types 中高相似度集中在 person 子类、location\n    子类； (3) n=27 per cell，power analysis 估计需 n≈80 才能在此效应量下达到 0.8 power。 这不是假设被否定——是实验\n    underpowered。但 median 档 reviewer 不会区分 \"underpowered  null\" 和 \"true null\"，会标注为\n    \"interaction claim not supported\"。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: 2×2 Interaction Design (Few-NERD F1)'\n    content: '|              | Low BCS | High BCS | BCS Δ  |\n\n      |--------------|---------|----------|--------|\n\n      | Count=6      | 0.324   | 0.313    | -0.011 |\n\n      | Count=12     | 0.325   | 0.277    | -0.048 |\n\n      | Count Δ      | +0.001  | -0.036   |        |\n\n      | Interaction: z=-0.67, p=0.50 (n.s.)        |\n\n      '\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Interaction plot: 两条线（low/high BCS）跨 count 水平，方向 non-parallel 但 CI 大量重叠'\n  analysis: '需要在论文中如实报告 null result 并提供 power analysis。FewRel 16→80 的 3.4×  amplification\n    作为 indirect interaction evidence。Reviewer 可能要求在 80-rel pool  上做正式 2×2 作为 rebuttal\n    补充分析。\n\n    '\n- name: Error Taxonomy\n  plan_id: exp-007\n  description: 系统性 FP 分类跨 BCS bins，multi-channel 机械性证据\n  expected_results:\n    fewnerd_intra_sub_by_bcs:\n      bcs_zero_pct: 0.0\n      bcs_low_pct: 1.6\n      bcs_medium_pct: 10.6\n      bcs_high_pct: 49.4\n      rho: 1.0\n      p: <0.001\n    fewrel_intra_sub_by_bcs:\n      bcs_zero_pct: 0.0\n      bcs_low_pct: 4.2\n      bcs_medium_pct: 13.0\n      bcs_high_pct: 20.3\n      bcs_very_high_pct: 32.3\n      rho: 0.954\n      p: <1e-6\n    cross_task:\n      ner_rho: 1.0\n      re_rho: 0.954\n    extra_sub: 0.0\n    hallucination_pct: <3%\n    missed_rate_range: 10-16%\n  result_rationale: 'Error taxonomy 是 median 档中最无争议的证据（A2 完全成立）。IntraSub 与 BCS 的  perfect/near-perfect\n    monotonic 关系直接验证了 multi-channel model 的核心机制： confusability 导致 type confusion（IntraSub）而非\n    detection failure（missed rate  不变 10-16%）。几个关键支撑点：(1) extra_sub=0，type confusion\n    严格是 intra-batch  现象，模型只从当前 schema 中选类型；(2) hallucination<3%，LLM 的主错误模式是  \"选错类型\"\n    而非 \"编造实体\"；(3) cross-task replication 几乎完美（NER ρ=1.0,  RE ρ=0.954），同一机制跨 NER 和\n    RE。即使在 median 档位，reviewer 也不会质疑这个分析。 这是论文的 \"safe anchor\"。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Error Taxonomy — Few-NERD (NER)'\n    content: '| BCS Bin  | N_FP | IntraSub% | ExtraSub% | Other%  |\n\n      |----------|------|-----------|-----------|---------|\n\n      | 0        | 6172 | 0.0       | 90.3      | 9.7     |\n\n      | Low      | 2231 | 1.6       | 89.9      | 8.5     |\n\n      | Medium   | 3843 | 10.6      | 78.1      | 11.3    |\n\n      | High     | 6188 | 49.4      | 30.8      | 19.8    |\n\n      '\n  - name: 'Table: Error Taxonomy — FewRel 80-rel (RE)'\n    content: '| BCS Bin    | Correct% | IntraSub% | Missed% |\n\n      |------------|----------|-----------|---------|\n\n      | Zero       | 85.7     | 0.0       | 14.3    |\n\n      | Low        | 85.4     | 4.2       | 10.4    |\n\n      | Medium     | 75.7     | 13.0      | 11.3    |\n\n      | High       | 66.7     | 20.3      | 13.0    |\n\n      | Very High  | 52.0     | 32.3      | 15.7    |\n\n      '\n  - name: 'Table: Cross-task Monotonicity'\n    content: '| Task | IntraSub vs BCS ρ | p       |\n\n      |------|-------------------|---------|\n\n      | NER  | 1.000             | <0.001  |\n\n      | RE   | 0.954             | <1e-6   |\n\n      '\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Stacked bar: FP composition 从 ExtraSub-dominant (BCS=0) 翻转为 IntraSub-dominant\n    (BCS>0.95)'\n  - 'Cross-task overlay: NER 和 RE IntraSub curves 近乎平行上升'\n  analysis: '论文最强的机械性证据，也是 Claim 2 的核心支撑。Cross-task ρ={1.0, 0.954} 是整篇论文 中最具说服力的数字。Median\n    档 reviewer 对此无异议。建议在论文中将此作为 Section 4  的第一个分析呈现（先建立机制理解，再展示 pairwise/scaling 证据）。\n\n    '\n- name: SDGD-zero on MAVEN\n  plan_id: exp-009\n  description: SDGD-zero 在 MAVEN 168 event types 上测试，对比 single-pass + random\n  expected_results:\n    single_pass:\n      relaxed_f1: 0.247\n      precision: 0.32\n      recall: 0.2\n      batches: 1\n      time_s: 130\n    random_batch:\n      relaxed_f1: 0.175\n      precision: 0.14\n      recall: 0.23\n      batches: 12\n      time_s: 950\n    sdgd_zero:\n      relaxed_f1: 0.135\n      precision: 0.12\n      recall: 0.155\n      batches: 8\n      time_s: 680\n    per_type:\n      relaxed_f1: 0.11\n      precision: 0.07\n      recall: 0.3\n      batches: 168\n      time_s: 9200\n  result_rationale: 'MAVEN 168 types 使所有 decomposition 方法的表现更差，原因层叠：(1) 168 types\n    产生  更多 batches，每次 merge 引入更多冲突——merge amplification 与 batch 数量超线性增长； (2) MAVEN\n    event types 语义高度同质（均为 FrameNet 层级，SCS mean=0.216,  119 pairs>0.5），SDGD-zero 的\n    graph coloring 无法有效分离——色数极高，被迫使用  大量 small batches 或在同 batch 内保留高 SCS pairs；(3)\n    event trigger boundary  本身模糊（exact F1 仅 0.01-0.03），decomposition 后 merge 多个 batch\n    的 trigger  predictions 进一步恶化边界匹配。SDGD-zero F1=0.135 vs single-pass 0.247，退化比 (0.55)\n    与 Few-NERD 上一致 (0.24/0.45=0.53)。Random batch 再次优于 SDGD-zero  (0.175 vs 0.135)——SDGD\n    的不均匀 batch size 在 MAVEN 上伤害更大。Per-type (168 batches)  recall 最高但 precision 崩溃（0.07），9200s\n    延迟不可接受。 Median 档位下，此实验巩固 \"merge amplification 是跨任务的结构性障碍\"，但同时加深  \"no practical\n    method\" 这一 major weakness。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: SDGD Comparison — MAVEN 168 types'\n    content: '| Method      | Relaxed F1 | P     | R     | k   | Time(s) |\n\n      |-------------|------------|-------|-------|-----|---------|\n\n      | Single-pass | 0.247      | 0.320 | 0.200 | 1   | 130     |\n\n      | Random      | 0.175      | 0.140 | 0.230 | 12  | 950     |\n\n      | SDGD-zero   | 0.135      | 0.120 | 0.155 | 8   | 680     |\n\n      | Per-type    | 0.110      | 0.070 | 0.300 | 168 | 9200    |\n\n      '\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Bar chart: single-pass 大幅领先，所有 decomposition 方法均为负面'\n  - 'Cross-dataset comparison: Few-NERD vs MAVEN decomposition penalty 一致'\n  analysis: '与 Few-NERD 模式完全一致。论文中应将 Few-NERD + MAVEN 的 SDGD 负面结果并排呈现， 强调 \"decomposition\n    penalty 是 task-agnostic 的结构性问题\"。同时明确指出 merge  strategy 是瓶颈（不是 grouping quality），为\n    future work 指明方向。Reviewer 的核心 质疑仍然是 \"如果你的方法不 work，这篇论文的 practical value 是什么？\"。\n\n    '\n- name: SDGD-cal on Few-NERD\n  plan_id: exp-010\n  description: 基于 5-10 个 calibration examples 的 empirical confusability graph，对比 SDGD-zero\n  expected_results:\n    sdgd_cal_5shot:\n      f1: 0.295\n      precision: 0.34\n      recall: 0.26\n      batches: 5\n      time_s: 370\n      calibration_overhead_s: 50\n    sdgd_cal_10shot:\n      f1: 0.315\n      precision: 0.36\n      recall: 0.28\n      batches: 5\n      time_s: 370\n      calibration_overhead_s: 90\n    vs_baselines:\n      sdgd_zero_f1: 0.241\n      random_batch_f1: 0.301\n      single_pass_f1: 0.445\n      cal5_vs_zero_pp: '+5.4'\n      cal10_vs_zero_pp: '+7.4'\n      cal10_vs_single_pass_pp: '-13.0'\n  result_rationale: 'Calibration 用 empirical confusion matrix 替代 embedding SCS，绕过了\n    embedding  选择问题，直接捕捉模型实际 confusion pattern。改善来源：(1) empirical confusion  比 SCS\n    更准确地识别 true confusion pairs（SCS 只解释 ~3% 方差，empirical 解释更多）； (2) 基于实际错误的 graph\n    更 sparse（大部分 type pairs 从不 confused），graph coloring  产生更均衡的 batches。但仍远低于 single-pass\n    (-13pp) 的原因不变：merge amplification  与 grouping quality 关系不大，是 decomposition 本身的结构性问题——即使完美分组避免了  所有\n    confusion pairs，合并多个 batch 的输出时同一 span 仍会被多个 batch \"认领\"。 5-shot vs 10-shot 差异小（0.295\n    vs 0.315），因为 5 个样本已识别出主要 confusion  clusters（person 子类、location 子类）。Median 档位下，SDGD-cal\n    展示了 \"right  direction\" 但 Δ=+7pp 不构成 practical improvement，reviewer 评价 \"interesting  diagnostically\n    but not actionable\"。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: SDGD-cal vs Baselines (Few-NERD)'\n    content: '| Method        | F1    | P     | R     | k | Extra(s) |\n\n      |---------------|-------|-------|-------|---|----------|\n\n      | Single-pass   | 0.445 | 0.563 | 0.368 | 1 | 0        |\n\n      | Random        | 0.301 | 0.331 | 0.276 | 8 | 0        |\n\n      | SDGD-zero     | 0.241 | 0.324 | 0.191 | 4 | 0        |\n\n      | SDGD-cal (5)  | 0.295 | 0.340 | 0.260 | 5 | 50       |\n\n      | SDGD-cal (10) | 0.315 | 0.360 | 0.280 | 5 | 90       |\n\n      '\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Bar chart: F1 阶梯 SDGD-zero < SDGD-cal ≈ Random << Single-pass'\n  - 'Precision-Recall scatter: 所有 decomposition 方法位于 single-pass 的 Pareto 劣势区'\n  analysis: 'SDGD-cal ≈ Random batch 的事实 is telling：即使用最好的 grouping signal，结果也不比 随机好多少。这进一步证实瓶颈是\n    merge 不是 grouping。论文中应明确写出这个 implication。 Reviewer 的追问：\"为什么不探索 confidence-weighted\n    merge / NMS-style 去重？\"—— 这是合理的 future work 方向，v2 已尝试 confidence-gated 但未奏效，说明问题比  simple\n    filtering 更深。\n\n    '\n- name: SDGD-cal on MAVEN\n  plan_id: exp-011\n  description: SDGD-cal 在 MAVEN 168 types 上的表现\n  expected_results:\n    sdgd_cal_5shot:\n      relaxed_f1: 0.165\n      precision: 0.15\n      recall: 0.185\n      batches: 10\n      calibration_overhead_s: 200\n    sdgd_cal_10shot:\n      relaxed_f1: 0.18\n      precision: 0.17\n      recall: 0.195\n      batches: 10\n      calibration_overhead_s: 380\n    vs_baselines:\n      single_pass_f1: 0.247\n      sdgd_zero_f1: 0.135\n      cal10_vs_zero_pp: '+4.5'\n      cal10_vs_single_pass_pp: '-6.7'\n  result_rationale: 'MAVEN 上 calibration 的边际改善比 Few-NERD 更小（+4.5pp vs +7.4pp），原因：\n    (1) 168 types 的 confusion space 更大（14028 pairs），5-10 个 calibration samples  覆盖率更低——每个\n    sample 最多涉及 ~10 types，需要 O(168) 个 samples 才能充分覆盖； (2) MAVEN 语义同质性导致 confusion\n    graph 极其 dense（几乎所有 type pairs 都有非零  confusion），graph coloring 的 chromatic number\n    很高，无论怎么分组都有大量 high-SCS  pairs 共存；(3) 200-380s 的 calibration overhead 在 168 types\n    上不可忽略，但换来的  仅 4.5pp 改善，投资回报率极低。SDGD-cal 仍远低于 single-pass (-6.7pp)。 Cross-task\n    一致的负面结果强化了结论，但也强化了 \"no practical method\" 的弱点。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: SDGD-cal vs Baselines (MAVEN)'\n    content: '| Method        | Relaxed F1 | k  | Calibration(s) |\n\n      |---------------|------------|----|----------------|\n\n      | Single-pass   | 0.247      | 1  | 0              |\n\n      | Random        | 0.175      | 12 | 0              |\n\n      | SDGD-zero     | 0.135      | 8  | 0              |\n\n      | SDGD-cal (5)  | 0.165      | 10 | 200            |\n\n      | SDGD-cal (10) | 0.180      | 10 | 380            |\n\n      '\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Cross-dataset SDGD comparison: Few-NERD 和 MAVEN bar charts 并排，模式一致'\n  analysis: '建议在论文中将 exp-009 和 exp-011 合并为一个 \"SDGD Results\" subsection，呈现  cross-task\n    一致的 hierarchy: single-pass > random ≈ cal > zero。 明确定位为 \"negative result with\n    diagnostic value\"——理解 WHY decomposition fails  本身是贡献，指向 calibration-aware merge\n    (非 calibration-aware grouping) 作为  correct next step。\n\n    '\n- name: Random Batching Ablation\n  plan_id: exp-013\n  description: 与 SDGD 相同 batch count k 的 random composition，隔离 confusability-aware\n    grouping 的增量\n  expected_results:\n    fewnerd_k4:\n      random_f1: 0.305\n      sdgd_zero_f1: 0.241\n      delta_pp: '+6.4'\n    fewnerd_k8:\n      random_f1: 0.295\n      sdgd_zero_f1: 0.22\n      delta_pp: '+7.5'\n    maven_k8:\n      random_f1: 0.175\n      sdgd_zero_f1: 0.135\n      delta_pp: '+4.0'\n    single_pass_f1_fewnerd: 0.445\n    single_pass_f1_maven: 0.247\n  result_rationale: 'Random batching 在所有条件下优于 SDGD-zero，看似反直觉但有清晰解释： (1) SDGD-zero\n    的 graph coloring + min_batch_size 约束产生高度不均匀的 batch sizes—— 某些 batch 仅含 3-4 types，prompt\n    中类型太少时模型缺乏任务范围 context，对每个类型  过度 predict（high recall, terrible precision）；random\n    batching 的 batch size 更均匀， 避免了这一退化模式；(2) SDGD-zero 将所有 \"hard\" (high-SCS) types\n    集中到同一个  batch，这些 batch 的 precision 崩溃；random 分散了 hard pairs，每个 batch 混合  easy+hard，整体更\n    balanced；(3) confusability-aware grouping 的正确 operationalization  应是 \"将 confusable\n    pairs 分开\"，但 SDGD-zero 的贪心 coloring 在约束下反而集中了  难题。这说明 SDGD-zero 的分组算法有 design flaw，不否定\n    confusability signal 本身。 Median 档位下，\"SDGD-zero < random\" 是 reviewer 最容易攻击的点之一。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Random vs SDGD-zero Ablation'\n    content: '| Dataset  | k | Random F1 | SDGD-zero F1 | Single-pass F1 |\n\n      |----------|---|-----------|--------------|----------------|\n\n      | Few-NERD | 4 | 0.305     | 0.241        | 0.445          |\n\n      | Few-NERD | 8 | 0.295     | 0.220        | 0.445          |\n\n      | MAVEN    | 8 | 0.175     | 0.135        | 0.247          |\n\n      '\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Bar chart: 三组对比（k=4, k=8, MAVEN k=8），random 始终优于 SDGD-zero'\n  analysis: '关键 takeaway 不是 \"confusability-aware grouping 无用\"，而是 \"当前的 SDGD-zero  实现的分组策略有副作用（batch\n    size 不均匀、hard type 集中化）抵消了 grouping 收益\"。 论文应 (1) 诚实报告 random > SDGD-zero；(2) 分析原因（batch\n    size distribution,  hard-batch concentration）；(3) 指出 all decomposition << single-pass，真正的瓶颈是  merge\n    不是 grouping。Reviewer 可能追问 \"为什么不修复 SDGD 的 batch size 问题？\"—— 合理的 rebuttal 是 exp-010\n    的 SDGD-cal 部分解决了这个问题但仍低于 single-pass。\n\n    '\n- name: Per-type Splitting (UniNER-style)\n  plan_id: exp-014\n  description: 每 batch 仅含 1 type，decomposition 的理论上限\n  expected_results:\n    fewnerd:\n      f1: 0.29\n      precision: 0.195\n      recall: 0.585\n      batches: 66\n      time_s: 2550\n      intra_sub_rate: 0.0\n      recall_vs_single_pass_pp: '+21.7'\n      precision_vs_single_pass_pp: '-36.8'\n      f1_vs_single_pass_pp: '-15.5'\n    maven:\n      relaxed_f1: 0.145\n      precision: 0.085\n      recall: 0.46\n      batches: 168\n      time_s: 9500\n  result_rationale: 'Per-type splitting 完全消除了 type confusion (IntraSub=0)——每个 batch\n    只有一个类型， 不可能把 entity 标为 \"wrong\" type。这验证了 multi-channel model 的 Channel 1 预测： Recall\n    从 0.368 跃升至 0.585 (+21.7pp)，因为每个 prompt 只需关注一个类型， attention 不被稀释，不遗漏。但 Precision\n    从 0.563 崩溃到 0.195 (-36.8pp)—— 66 个 batch 的 union merge 引入大量冲突：同一 text span 被 person-scholar、\n    person-scientist、person-other 各自 \"认领\"，union merge 保留所有 predictions， precision\n    崩溃。F1 净效果为负 (-15.5pp)。 MAVEN 168 types 更极端——recall 高但 precision 更低（0.085），因为 168\n    个 single-type  batch 的 merge 冲突呈 O(k²) 增长。 这清晰展示了 decomposition 的 fundamental\n    tradeoff：分解减少 miss (Channel 1 benefit)， 但 merge 产生 false positives (new Channel\n    3 problem)。当前所有 merge strategy  （union, confidence-gated）都不能解决 O(k) batches 的冲突。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Full Decomposition Spectrum (Few-NERD)'\n    content: '| Method      | F1    | P     | R     | k  | IntraSub | Time(s) |\n\n      |-------------|-------|-------|-------|----|----------|---------|\n\n      | Single-pass | 0.445 | 0.563 | 0.368 | 1  | baseline | 79      |\n\n      | Random (k=8)| 0.295 | 0.330 | 0.270 | 8  | moderate | 494     |\n\n      | SDGD-zero   | 0.241 | 0.324 | 0.191 | 4  | low      | 261     |\n\n      | SDGD-cal    | 0.315 | 0.360 | 0.280 | 5  | low      | 460     |\n\n      | Per-type    | 0.290 | 0.195 | 0.585 | 66 | 0        | 2550    |\n\n      '\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Precision-Recall tradeoff: per-type 在 high-recall/low-precision 极端，single-pass\n    在 balanced 区'\n  - 'Stacked bar: recall gain vs precision loss，per-type 的 precision loss 完全 dominate'\n  analysis: 'Per-type 的 recall 优势是 decomposition 正确直觉的最好证据——问题确实在 merge。 论文结构建议：先展示\n    per-type 的 recall gain (证明 decomposition 有理论价值)， 再展示所有方法的 precision collapse (证明\n    merge amplification 是瓶颈)， 最后指出 \"future work needs better merge, not better grouping\"。\n    Reviewer 会欣赏这个清晰的 ablation 分析。1-2 位 reviewer 仍会标注 \"the paper  identifies the problem\n    but doesn''t solve it\" 作为 major weakness，这是 median 档 避不开的。\n\n    '\n- name: SCS Validation\n  plan_id: exp-015\n  description: Spearman/Kendall correlation between embedding SCS 和 empirical confusion\n    matrix\n  expected_results:\n    all_pairs:\n      n: 1953\n      qwen3_spearman: 0.168\n      qwen3_p: '7.3e-14'\n      qwen3_kendall: 0.135\n      minilm_spearman: 0.144\n      minilm_p: '1.7e-10'\n      minilm_kendall: 0.115\n    nonzero_only:\n      n: 216\n      qwen3_spearman: 0.272\n      qwen3_p: '5.0e-5'\n      qwen3_kendall: 0.2\n      minilm_spearman: 0.306\n      minilm_p: '4.6e-6'\n      minilm_kendall: 0.228\n    variance_explained:\n      all_pairs_r_squared: 2.8-4.8%\n      nonzero_r_squared: 7.4-9.4%\n  result_rationale: 'SCS 是有效但不完美的 confusion proxy。All-pairs ρ 偏低（0.14-0.17）的根本原因是  data\n    极度 zero-inflated：88.9% 的 type pairs 从未被混淆（confusion=0），产生大量  ties 压缩 rank correlation。Nonzero-only\n    ρ 跳升到 0.27-0.31，说明 SCS 能有效区分  \"哪些 pairs 被混淆得更多\" 但不太能预测 \"哪些 pairs 会被混淆\"。 Qwen3\n    在 all-pairs 上更好（ρ=0.168 vs 0.144）——extraction model 的 embedding  更好地捕捉 \"是否会混淆\"\n    的 threshold，因为 embedding space 与 model 的 internal  representation 对齐。MiniLM 在\n    nonzero-only 上更好（ρ=0.306 vs 0.272）——sentence  similarity model 的 fine-grained\n    similarity gradient 更平滑，更好地排序 confusion  程度。 Median 档位下，reviewer 的主要质疑是 R²=3-5%：如果你的\n    proxy 只解释 3-5% 的方差， 基于它构建的 SDGD 分组怎么可能有效？这恰好与 SDGD-zero 的失败一致——SCS 作为 grouping  signal\n    太 noisy。论文应将此定位为 \"validating the existence of the signal\" 而非  \"validating its\n    practical sufficiency\"，并指向 SDGD-cal (empirical confusion)  作为正确的 operationalization\n    路径。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: SCS → Empirical Confusion Validation'\n    content: '| Subset        | Embedding | Spearman ρ | p        | Kendall τ | R²     |\n\n      |---------------|-----------|------------|----------|-----------|--------|\n\n      | All (n=1953)  | Qwen3     | 0.168      | 7.3e-14  | 0.135     | ~4.8%  |\n\n      | All (n=1953)  | MiniLM    | 0.144      | 1.7e-10  | 0.115     | ~2.8%  |\n\n      | Nonzero (216) | Qwen3     | 0.272      | 5.0e-5   | 0.200     | ~7.4%  |\n\n      | Nonzero (216) | MiniLM    | 0.306      | 4.6e-6   | 0.228     | ~9.4%  |\n\n      '\n  figures_description:\n  - 'SCS vs confusion scatter: 大量零值集中在 x 轴，nonzero 区域显示 positive trend'\n  - 'Embedding 对比: Qwen3 vs MiniLM 的 SCS-confusion curves 在 nonzero 区域交叉'\n  analysis: SCS validation 支撑了 \"confusability signal exists\" 但也暴露了 \"signal is weak\n    for  practical use\"。这与 SDGD 的负面结果形成一致叙事：pairwise SCS 作为分析工具有效 （cross-task 显著），作为工程工具不足（R²太低）。论文应诚实呈现这个\n    gap，并将  SDGD-cal (bypassing embedding entirely) 作为 pragmatic 替代方案。 Reviewer 可能追问\n    AUC（SCS 预测 nonzero confusion 的分类能力），预估 AUC≈0.65-0.70， 属于 \"above chance but far\n    from reliable\" 水平。\n","numLines":564,"startLine":1,"totalLines":564}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01DjXqWvgrjNs1yMKHCGYifL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I've read both the PDF paper and the review context YAML. Now I need to conduct a full DREAM review with the dispatch template: 2 Reviewers (R1 for methods+experiments, R2 for novelty+related work), followed by a complete roundtable (Step 1 independent → Step 2 cross-sharing → Step 3 convergence → Step 4 synthesis).\n\nLet me launch R1 and R2 as parallel agents for Step 1 (independent reviews), then proceed through the roundtable steps.\n\nLet me summarize what I've learned from the paper and context:\n\n**Paper**: \"Multi-Channel Schema Degradation in Training-Free LLM Information Extraction: A Controlled Empirical Study\"\n\n\nThe core contribution is a multi-channel degradation model showing how count and confusability independently drive performance decline, validated through error taxonomy analysis across NER and RE tasks with near-perfect monotonic relationships, though the proposed decomposition approach underperforms single-pass baselines across all tested methods.\n\nNow I'm checking which experiments from the planned list made it into the final paper — most of the key ablations are there, including the confusability study, interaction effects, error taxonomy, and the SDGD variants across different datasets and calibration settings.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":32775,"cache_read_input_tokens":22928,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":32775},"output_tokens":18,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b735db44-76af-4d42-8a6c-987fd4628342","uuid":"d0010192-39aa-4328-b247-37d3aad1c2aa"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01DjXqWvgrjNs1yMKHCGYifL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have the paper and review context. Launching R1 (methods + experiments) and R2 (novelty + related work) in parallel for Step 1 independent reviews."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":32775,"cache_read_input_tokens":22928,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":32775},"output_tokens":18,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b735db44-76af-4d42-8a6c-987fd4628342","uuid":"c57044c3-38a9-4100-ab88-d132a146b149"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01DjXqWvgrjNs1yMKHCGYifL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01V8q1GFnKvDYdk5w2zPN6Tk","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"R1: Methods + Experiments review","prompt":"You are Reviewer R1 for a top ML venue review. Your focus is **methods and experiments**. Review the paper below using a 6-point scale (1=Strong Reject, 2=Reject, 3=Weak Reject, 4=Weak Accept, 5=Accept, 6=Strong Accept). Target venue acceptance rate ~25%.\n\n## Paper Summary\n\n**Title**: \"Multi-Channel Schema Degradation in Training-Free LLM Information Extraction: A Controlled Empirical Study\"\n\nThe paper studies why training-free LLM-based IE degrades as schema complexity increases. It proposes a \"multi-channel degradation model\" isolating two factors:\n- **Channel 1 (Count → Recall Decline)**: More types → attention dilution → entity omission\n- **Channel 2 (Confusability → Type Confusion)**: Semantically similar co-present types → intra-batch substitution errors\n\n**Key experimental results**:\n\n1. **Error Taxonomy** (Tables 1-2): On Few-NERD NER, IntraSub rises from 0% (zero BCS) to 49.4% (high BCS) with ρ=1.0. On FewRel RE, same pattern with ρ=0.954. Missed rate stays in 10-16% band regardless of BCS. ExtraSub=0% always. Cross-task monotonicity Table 3 confirms.\n\n2. **DocRED Confusability Study** (Tables 4-5): 96 relation types. Count curve shows 42pp degradation (0.74→0.32). BCS-controlled: at count=16, high-BCS is 16pp lower (ρ=-0.42, p=0.028); at count=32, Δ=-13pp (p=0.055, borderline). Pairwise r=0.09 (CI [0.04, 0.14]).\n\n3. **SCS Validation** (Table 6): Embedding-based SCS validated against empirical confusion matrix on Few-NERD. All-pairs: Qwen3 ρ=0.168, MiniLM ρ=0.144 (both p<10^-10). R²≈3-5% all pairs, 7-9% nonzero-only. Paper says R²=3-9% in abstract.\n\n4. **2×2 Interaction** (Table 7): {low/high count} × {low/high BCS} on Few-NERD. BCS effect 4.4× larger at count=12 vs count=6, but interaction n.s. (z=-0.67, p=0.50). Paper acknowledges underpowered (n=27 per cell, needs n≈80).\n\n5. **SDGD-zero + Random on MAVEN** (Tables 8-9): Single-pass F1=0.247 > Random 0.175 > SDGD-zero 0.135 > Per-type 0.110. Random outperforms SDGD-zero by 4-7.5pp across datasets.\n\n6. **SDGD-cal** (Tables 10-11): On Few-NERD, SDGD-cal(10) F1=0.315, still 13pp below single-pass 0.445. On MAVEN, SDGD-cal(10) relaxed F1=0.180, 6.7pp below single-pass. SDGD-cal ≈ random batching.\n\n7. **Per-type splitting** (Table 12): Recall jumps +21.7pp but precision collapses -36.8pp. F1 net -15.5pp. IntraSub=0 as expected.\n\n**Setup**: Qwen3-32B, zero-shot. Datasets: Few-NERD (66 NER types), FewRel (80 RE types), DocRED (96 RE types), MAVEN (168 ED types). Metrics: span F1 for NER, accuracy for RE, relaxed F1 for ED.\n\n## Your Task\n\nEvaluate the **methodological rigor** and **experimental design**. Produce a structured review with:\n\n1. **Summary** (2-3 sentences)\n2. **Strengths** (bulleted, focus on experimental design, controls, statistical rigor)\n3. **Weaknesses** (bulleted, focus on methodological gaps, confounds, missing controls, statistical issues)\n4. **Questions for Authors** (numbered)\n5. **Minor Issues** (if any)\n6. **Overall Assessment** (1 paragraph)\n7. **Scores**: Overall (1-6), Soundness (1-4), Confidence (1-5)\n\nKey methodological questions to consider:\n- Is the count vs confusability isolation clean? Could there be confounds?\n- Is single-model (Qwen3-32B only) sufficient for generalizability?\n- The interaction test is underpowered (p=0.50) — how much does this weaken the \"orthogonal channels\" claim?\n- DocRED count=32 p=0.055 borderline — cherry-picking concern?\n- SCS R²=3-5% — does this undermine the practical utility claim?\n- All decomposition methods fail — is the paper \"identifying a problem without solving it\"?\n- Merge strategy is only union+deduplication — were alternatives explored?\n- No confidence intervals or error bars reported on F1/accuracy numbers\n- Only one LLM tested — would results hold for GPT-4, Claude, Llama?\n- FewRel uses \"accuracy\" while others use F1 — metric inconsistency?\n\nBe rigorous and specific. Cite table/section numbers.","model":"sonnet"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":32775,"cache_read_input_tokens":22928,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":32775},"output_tokens":18,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b735db44-76af-4d42-8a6c-987fd4628342","uuid":"916eaa65-3303-4211-a5d3-3a2bbfa0882c"}
{"type":"system","subtype":"task_started","task_id":"a44ffc07eb6b20bad","tool_use_id":"toolu_01V8q1GFnKvDYdk5w2zPN6Tk","description":"R1: Methods + Experiments review","task_type":"local_agent","prompt":"You are Reviewer R1 for a top ML venue review. Your focus is **methods and experiments**. Review the paper below using a 6-point scale (1=Strong Reject, 2=Reject, 3=Weak Reject, 4=Weak Accept, 5=Accept, 6=Strong Accept). Target venue acceptance rate ~25%.\n\n## Paper Summary\n\n**Title**: \"Multi-Channel Schema Degradation in Training-Free LLM Information Extraction: A Controlled Empirical Study\"\n\nThe paper studies why training-free LLM-based IE degrades as schema complexity increases. It proposes a \"multi-channel degradation model\" isolating two factors:\n- **Channel 1 (Count → Recall Decline)**: More types → attention dilution → entity omission\n- **Channel 2 (Confusability → Type Confusion)**: Semantically similar co-present types → intra-batch substitution errors\n\n**Key experimental results**:\n\n1. **Error Taxonomy** (Tables 1-2): On Few-NERD NER, IntraSub rises from 0% (zero BCS) to 49.4% (high BCS) with ρ=1.0. On FewRel RE, same pattern with ρ=0.954. Missed rate stays in 10-16% band regardless of BCS. ExtraSub=0% always. Cross-task monotonicity Table 3 confirms.\n\n2. **DocRED Confusability Study** (Tables 4-5): 96 relation types. Count curve shows 42pp degradation (0.74→0.32). BCS-controlled: at count=16, high-BCS is 16pp lower (ρ=-0.42, p=0.028); at count=32, Δ=-13pp (p=0.055, borderline). Pairwise r=0.09 (CI [0.04, 0.14]).\n\n3. **SCS Validation** (Table 6): Embedding-based SCS validated against empirical confusion matrix on Few-NERD. All-pairs: Qwen3 ρ=0.168, MiniLM ρ=0.144 (both p<10^-10). R²≈3-5% all pairs, 7-9% nonzero-only. Paper says R²=3-9% in abstract.\n\n4. **2×2 Interaction** (Table 7): {low/high count} × {low/high BCS} on Few-NERD. BCS effect 4.4× larger at count=12 vs count=6, but interaction n.s. (z=-0.67, p=0.50). Paper acknowledges underpowered (n=27 per cell, needs n≈80).\n\n5. **SDGD-zero + Random on MAVEN** (Tables 8-9): Single-pass F1=0.247 > Random 0.175 > SDGD-zero 0.135 > Per-type 0.110. Random outperforms SDGD-zero by 4-7.5pp across datasets.\n\n6. **SDGD-cal** (Tables 10-11): On Few-NERD, SDGD-cal(10) F1=0.315, still 13pp below single-pass 0.445. On MAVEN, SDGD-cal(10) relaxed F1=0.180, 6.7pp below single-pass. SDGD-cal ≈ random batching.\n\n7. **Per-type splitting** (Table 12): Recall jumps +21.7pp but precision collapses -36.8pp. F1 net -15.5pp. IntraSub=0 as expected.\n\n**Setup**: Qwen3-32B, zero-shot. Datasets: Few-NERD (66 NER types), FewRel (80 RE types), DocRED (96 RE types), MAVEN (168 ED types). Metrics: span F1 for NER, accuracy for RE, relaxed F1 for ED.\n\n## Your Task\n\nEvaluate the **methodological rigor** and **experimental design**. Produce a structured review with:\n\n1. **Summary** (2-3 sentences)\n2. **Strengths** (bulleted, focus on experimental design, controls, statistical rigor)\n3. **Weaknesses** (bulleted, focus on methodological gaps, confounds, missing controls, statistical issues)\n4. **Questions for Authors** (numbered)\n5. **Minor Issues** (if any)\n6. **Overall Assessment** (1 paragraph)\n7. **Scores**: Overall (1-6), Soundness (1-4), Confidence (1-5)\n\nKey methodological questions to consider:\n- Is the count vs confusability isolation clean? Could there be confounds?\n- Is single-model (Qwen3-32B only) sufficient for generalizability?\n- The interaction test is underpowered (p=0.50) — how much does this weaken the \"orthogonal channels\" claim?\n- DocRED count=32 p=0.055 borderline — cherry-picking concern?\n- SCS R²=3-5% — does this undermine the practical utility claim?\n- All decomposition methods fail — is the paper \"identifying a problem without solving it\"?\n- Merge strategy is only union+deduplication — were alternatives explored?\n- No confidence intervals or error bars reported on F1/accuracy numbers\n- Only one LLM tested — would results hold for GPT-4, Claude, Llama?\n- FewRel uses \"accuracy\" while others use F1 — metric inconsistency?\n\nBe rigorous and specific. Cite table/section numbers.","uuid":"fd5f8edb-7403-47a9-b36f-e7296ce75502","session_id":"b735db44-76af-4d42-8a6c-987fd4628342"}
